  "scientific_simplifications": [
    "Only one duplicated chromosome (one sister chromatid pair) is modeled, instantiating the source's universal alignment statement for that single pair.",
    "Separation is shown as the joined pair splitting into two persistent chromatids (each now called a chromosome); post-separation identity preserved via origin_id and semantic_state_alias.",
    "Molecular cohesin degradation/cleavage mechanism is NOT shown; only observable connection breakdown and separation are depicted.",
    "Stages are discrete and schematic; phase order is schematic, not a strict per-chromosome causal prerequisite.",
    "Maximal chromosome condensation at metaphase is out of scope and not depicted as a process effect."
